        "original_id": "9456d194-c2cc-562e-9da6-509caac93a3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ziggy Marley, Flea, John Frusciante, Michael Peter Balzary\n- Music Groups: Red Hot Chili Peppers, Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers\n- Albums: Dragonfly, Love Is My Religion\n- Songs: Rainbow in the Sky, Melancholy Mood\n\nFacts:\n- Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers ended in 2000.\n- Dragonfly was Ziggy Marley's first solo album after the 2000 end of Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers.\n- Love Is My Religion was Ziggy Marley's second solo album, following Dragonfly.\n- The song \"Rainbow in the Sky\" on Dragonfly features Flea and John Frusciante of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- The song \"Melancholy Mood\" on Dragonfly features Flea but not John Frusciante.\n- Michael Peter Balzary, born on 16 October 1962 and known as Flea, is an Australian-American musician and actor.\n- Flea is best known as the bassist and a founding member of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
